Hi all.  I'm running the AMELIA II program through Amelia View in
order to impute some missing TSCS data.  The data are state-level
variables, running from 1980 to 2010.  I have 70 variables and only a
handful of them have significant missing data, often in the form of
data from decennial censuses (e.g. % urban) that are missing for the
intervening years.

I would like to set k=2 and interact the cross-sectional IDs with the
time spline.  The problem is that no matter how I set the interaction
(either clicking "interact spline with cross-section" or leaving it
un-clicked), the output log shows "intercs = FALSE".

Any ideas about what's going wrong?  I've posted the full output log
below for reference.

Also, I currently have the time variable in distance from the mean
year (e.g. -15 to 15) rather than in year numbers (e.g. 1980 to 2010).
 Is this the correct specification for time?

Many thanks,

Michelle Phelps
Ph.D. Candidate
Sociology & Social Policy
Princeton University


