Thanks for the response, Matt.  I had loaded the amelia package, but I just
forgot to copy and paste that into the code I submitted to the mailing
list.  Anyways, I was able to get the script working after some
adjustments.  Below is the working script:

library(Amelia)
library(mitools)
library(nlme)
library(mitools)
library(foreach)
library(doSNOW)
registerDoSNOW(makeCluster(7, type = "SOCK"))

ameliapar <- function(x, m=7, p2s=2, ...) {
  foreach (i = 1:m,
           .combine = "ameliabind",
           .packages="Amelia") %dopar% {
             amelia(x, m=1, p2s=p2s, ...)
           }
}

ameliapar(x = africa, m=7, cs = "country", ts = "year", logs = "gdp_pc")

Thanks for your help!

-Isaac


